  "interpretations": [
    "compute_qha_gibbs is the infimum over an open volume window of F(T,V)+pV, with F the actual molar Helmholtz surface of the static-plus-harmonic ensembles and x=(T,p).",
    "compute_heat_capacity_p is -T*(d2G/dT2)_p of that Gibbs energy; compute_thermal_expansion is (dV/dT)_p/V with V=(dG/dp)_T; compute_bulk_modulus_qha is V*(d2F/dV2)_T at the volume (dG/dp)_T.",
    "contract_thermal_gruneisen is the mean of supplied mode parameters weighted by actual Physlib canonical heat capacities of supplied oscillators.",
    "These producer definitions read nothing from the response quantities they are proved equal to: no expansion, bulk, cp, branch structure or mode-weighted Gamma appears in their closures.",
    "The identifications hold on a local stable equilibrium family for every sufficiently narrow window. Numerical volume scans, EOS fits, minimizers, FC3 and finite-difference Gruneisen producers and Phonopy are not verified."
